# Evaluator rubric

Use after implementation, before acceptance. The evaluator is not the agent
that wrote the code. Score 0–2; any 0 in a hard-threshold row blocks.

| Category | Question | Hard threshold | Score | Evidence (file:line, command output) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Correctness | Does the behaviour match the feature entry and spec? | Yes | | |
| Verification | Did the required checks actually run, in all required layers? | Yes | | |
| Scope discipline | Did the change stay inside the feature? | Yes | | |
| Reliability | Does it survive restart and re-run without repair? | Yes | | |
| Maintainability | Clear code, boundaries respected, docs updated? | No | | |
| Handoff readiness | Can a fresh session continue from repo files alone? | No | | |

## Verdict
- [ ] Accept  - [ ] Revise  - [ ] Block

## Required follow-up
- Missing evidence:
- Required fixes:
- Next review trigger:
